  "id": "a552cae9-7e5f-4b32-8bab-2b84db44f612",
  "title": "HDFC, ICICI Bank and Financial Institutions to File Prosecution Charges for Subvention Scheme Fraud",
  "summary": "The Supreme Court has directed HDFC Bank, ICICI Bank, Sammaan Capital, and PNB Housing Finance to grant unconditional sanction for prosecution of their officials within a week in alleged subvention scheme frauds involving real estate developers, banks, and financial institutions. The court warned that the heads of these institutions must personally appear before it in case of non-compliance, as the case revolves around financial misconduct.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Supreme Court directed HDFC Bank, ICICI Bank, Sammaan Capital, and PNB Housing Finance to file prosecution charges in subvention fraud cases involving real estate developers, banks, and financial institutions.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The court ordered the sanction of the financial institutions to proceed with prosecution within a week, with failure to do so resulting in the removal of the CMD and Chairman from the court.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The case involves alleged collusion between lenders and developers under home loan subvention schemes, which has led to financial distress for homebuyers.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
